# Medusa Modules Conventions

## Estrutura de Módulo

Cada módulo customizado deve seguir esta estrutura:

```
apps/medusa/src/modules/<module-name>/
├── index.ts                 # Export do módulo
├── service.ts               # Lógica de negócio
├── models/                  # Entidades/modelos
│   └── <entity>.ts
├── migrations/              # Migrations do banco
│   └── YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_<description>.ts
├── types/                   # Tipos específicos do módulo
│   └── index.ts
└── __tests__/               # Testes
    └── service.spec.ts
```

## Registrar Módulo

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - apps/medusa/src/modules/subscription/index.ts
import { Module } from '@medusajs/utils';
import { SubscriptionService } from './service';

export const SUBSCRIPTION_MODULE = 'subscriptionModuleService';

export default Module(SUBSCRIPTION_MODULE, {
  service: SubscriptionService,
});
```

## Service Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - service com injeção de dependências
import { MedusaContainer } from '@medusajs/types';

export class SubscriptionService {
  constructor(private readonly container: MedusaContainer) {}

  async createPlan(data: CreatePlanInput): Promise<SubscriptionPlan> {
    // validação
    // lógica de negócio
    // persistência
    return plan;
  }

  async cancelSubscription(id: string): Promise<void> {
    // lógica de cancelamento
  }
}
```

## Models

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - model com decorators do Medusa
import { model } from '@medusajs/utils';

@model()
export class SubscriptionPlan {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  price: number;
  interval: 'monthly' | 'yearly';
  features: string[];
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

## Migrations

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - migration com up/down
import { Migration } from '@medusajs/utils';

export default class CreateSubscriptionPlan1234567890 implements Migration {
  async up(): Promise<void> {
    await this.query(`
      CREATE TABLE subscription_plan (
        id VARCHAR PRIMARY KEY,
        name VARCHAR NOT NULL,
        price INTEGER NOT NULL,
        interval VARCHAR NOT NULL,
        created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
        updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
      )
    `);
  }

  async down(): Promise<void> {
    await this.query('DROP TABLE subscription_plan');
  }
}
```

## API Routes

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - admin route
// apps/medusa/src/api/admin/subscriptions/route.ts
import { MedusaRequest, MedusaResponse } from '@medusajs/medusa';

export async function POST(req: MedusaRequest, res: MedusaResponse) {
  const subscriptionService = req.scope.resolve('subscriptionModuleService');
  const plan = await subscriptionService.createPlan(req.body);
  res.json({ plan });
}

// ✅ BOM - store route
// apps/medusa/src/api/store/subscriptions/route.ts
export async function GET(req: MedusaRequest, res: MedusaResponse) {
  const subscriptionService = req.scope.resolve('subscriptionModuleService');
  const subscriptions = await subscriptionService.listByCustomer(req.user.id);
  res.json({ subscriptions });
}
```

## Testes

```typescript
// ✅ BOM - testes de service
describe('SubscriptionService', () => {
  let service: SubscriptionService;
  let container: MedusaContainer;

  beforeEach(() => {
    container = createMockContainer();
    service = new SubscriptionService(container);
  });

  describe('createPlan', () => {
    it('should create plan with valid data', async () => {
      const data = { name: 'Pro', price: 9900, interval: 'monthly' };
      const plan = await service.createPlan(data);
      expect(plan.name).toBe('Pro');
    });
  });
});
```

## Gotchas

- Migrations devem ter timestamp no nome
- Services devem ser registrados no container
- Use `MedusaRequest` e `MedusaResponse` para routes
- Models precisam do decorator `@model()`
- Sempre implemente `up` e `down` em migrations

Referência: [Medusa v2 Modules](https://docs.medusajs.com/v2/modules)
